  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper level low continues its \njourney around the PacNW, bringing cooler temperatures, strong \nwinds and precipitation potential. A strong pressure gradient is \ndeveloping across the area, resulting in strong winds across the \narea and temperatures ranging from the upper 60s in northern \nNevada to the low 80s in central Nevada. Strong winds are expected\nto continue through Sunday, particularly in White Pine, northeast\nNye and southeast Elko Counties. Moisture availability starting \nSunday has been trending downward the last several forecasts and \nprecipitation potential has noticeably decreased along with it. \nIsolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms continue to be \nforecast across much of the forecast area for Sunday but \naccumulation totals have dropped to 0.05 inches at best, with most\nof the area expecting a trace or less. Precipitation chances dry \nout by Monday morning, allowing a dry but cool day, with high \ntemperatures in the 70s. Unsettled weather is expected to continue\nfor mid week even as temperatures warm back into the 80s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in cool\ntemperatures and strong winds through the weekend. Weekend storm\nconfidence continues to be moderate, with low confidence in storm\npotential next week. No changes from the NBM.",
